## 📊 Architecture

### Authentication Flow

```
1. User visits website (localhost:3001)
2. Clicks "Get Started" → Redirects to dashboard signup (localhost:3000/signup)
3. Submits signup form → API (localhost:3333/api/auth/register)
4. API creates user, hashes password, returns JWT token
5. Dashboard stores token in localStorage
6. User redirected to dashboard (localhost:3000/dashboard)
7. Protected routes verify token before rendering
```

### Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| **Website** | Next.js 15, App Router, Tailwind CSS, Inter font |
| **Dashboard** | React 18, Vite, React Router 7, Tailwind CSS |
| **API** | NestJS 11, TypeScript, JWT, bcrypt |
| **Libraries** | Shared React components and utilities |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL 16 (in docker-compose) |
| **Cache** | Redis 7 (in docker-compose) |
| **E2E Testing** | Playwright with multi-browser support |
| **Build** | Nx 21, TypeScript 5.8 (strict mode) |
| **Containerization** | Docker multi-stage builds |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions |

